- [Testen mithilfe von Anfordern/Verpflichten](request-response-testing.md)--------------------            Debug.Assert(New_containsNewRet); 
        }

        public void PUT_SetContract([PexAssumeUnderTest]ArrayList arrList, int index, int value)
        {
            AssumePrecondition.IsTrue(index < arrList.Count && index >= 0);

            int Old_arrListCount = arrList.Count;
            int Old_index = index;
            int Old_value = (int)arrList[index];

            arrList[index] = value;

            int New_arrListCount = arrList.Count;
            int New_indexValue = (int)arrList[index];

            PexObserve.ValueForViewing("$old_arrList_Count", Old_arrListCount);
            PexObserve.ValueForViewing("$new_arrList_Count", New_arrListCount);
            PexObserve.ValueForViewing("$old_arrList_index", Old_index);
            PexObserve.ValueForViewing("$old_arrList_value", Old_value);
            PexObserve.ValueForViewing("$new_indexValue", New_indexValue);

            // an assertion using "Debug.Assert\(.*?\);" that  @@@ the newly set index value is equals to the input 'value'
            Debug.Assert(New_indexValue == value); 
        }
    }
}--------------------
            Debug.Assert((New_arrListCount == Old_arrListCount), "$new_arrList_Count is equal to $old_arrList_Count");
            Debug.Assert((New_containsNewRet), "$new_containsNewRet evaluates to true");
            Debug.Assert(((Old_index >= 0 ) && (Old_index < Old_arrListCount)), "$old_index is a legal index in the $old_arrList_Count");

        }
    }
}--------------------        }
    }
}
```

The `AssumePrecondition.IsTrue()` function makes sure that the index is within the bounds of actual elements in the ArrayList. This simplifies the Pex exploration by reducing the set of inputs to the function that Pex can explore.

Also note that in order for Pex to explore the possible outputs of the test, it is necessary to set the observed values for the viewer in the `PexObserve.ValueForViewing()` calls.

The second part of the method where we perform the `arrList[index]` operation and store it into the `New_Ret` variable. We also check if `New_Ret` is present in the list or not using the `arrList.Contains(New_Ret);` method.

Lastly the `Debug.Assert` line in C# is annotated to notify Pex that the array must contain New_Ret in order to pass the assertion.

The Pex framework analyzes the contract of the function ensuring that the contract is preserved after the operation being tested.

Note that this is an ideal example, and may not always be needed based on the actual function being tested. In general, the key is to ensure the conditions for a successful test are met before making the operation being tested.--------------------		
            AssertContract.True(New_containsNewRet);
        }
    }
}--------------------            Assert.IsTrue(arrList.Contains(New_Ret));
 
        }
    }
